# "Time and memory that lasts" — the save-slot statements. The first run
# finds no slot for game 42 and takes the lowest free one; the second finds
# it and loads the score back; then byte 3 of slot 0, the low half of the
# score, is changed without the check number and the third run finds the save
# damaged, erases it, and starts again in the same slot.
wait (OK|\?)
send 1500\r
send RUN\r
send 900\r
send NVRAM 3, NVRAM(3) + 1\r
send RUN\r
send 100\r
expect ^BEST SO FAR: 0$
expect ^A NEW BEST, IN SLOT 0$
expect ^BEST SO FAR: 1500$
expect ^NOT THIS TIME$
expect ^THE LAST SAVE WAS DAMAGED\nBEST SO FAR: 0$
